  "findings": [
    "General visibility filtering materially increases cost under this overlap workload",
    "The mostly-unbounded outdoor root domain still pays per-fragment envelope checks",
    "Simplifying root metadata lookup did not produce a repeatable speedup",
    "Replacing texture material with constant color alone barely reduced cost",
    "Disabling blending alone did not reduce cost",
    "Removing discard while retaining neutral transparent masking did not reduce cost",
    "Restricting rasterization to a central half-width half-height scissor reduced GPU cost substantially with unchanged geometry/draw counts",
    "No production source files were edited"
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "GPU phase sums overlap CPU work and are not end-to-end frame latency",
    "Variants that bypass portals or change material/blending alter output and are diagnostic only",
    "Scissor variant performs synchronous state queries and must not be used to infer CPU or FPS improvement",
    "Overlap counters capture adjacent frames and use an RGBA32F additive counter; they measure depth-passing coverage, not hardware fragment-invocation or occupancy counters",
    "Simplified root predicate was numerically compared on one captured frame: zero mismatches; this is not general visual acceptance",
    "Transparent masking test checks neutral blend-factor preconditions but has no visual acceptance claim",
    "A spatial fast path that avoids envelope reads outside portal-affected regions is an unmeasured next experiment; it must be derived conservatively from the frame plan"
  ]
